     1	## E42 The F3 starter project: one dataset through the whole chain, judged against dGB's own survey — QUEUED (after E41 and the Ophiolite half; before E43's real-data acceptance and E44; Kernel, cross-repo; strategy at lane open; one Codex round)
     2	
     3	Authority: owner direction 28 Oct 2026 ("F3 for us may be a useful test case to try and replicate as
     4	a proof of concept"; OSD-D21); family rules R-T1 to R-T5 and R-T7; E40 (starter/1), E41 (F3
     5	deposited and at L2), E07 (mirror and custody); Ophiolite E125 (OpendTect connector over odbind,
     6	merged 22 Oct), E126 (notebook adapters and gallery, merged 22 Oct), E85 (one intake); the Ophiolite
     7	half chartered from `E42-ophiolite-half.md`; Ophiolite R-C1.
     8	
     9	**Outcome.** A person opens opensubsurfacedata.org, finds F3 (Dutch North Sea), and downloads a
    10	starter project for OpendTect, for ResInsight or for Python. The OpendTect pack opens as a survey
    11	with the F3 cube, the four wells with their logs and the horizons, in the right place, in metres,
    12	in time, under CC BY-SA 3.0 with dGB named. The ResInsight pack opens as a project with the four
    13	well paths and logs and, if ResInsight's API imports it, the cube. The Python pack is a notebook
    14	that reads the same data through standard libraries and plots one inline with the wells on it.
    15	Each pack ships its decision log and its fidelity record, and the catalogue shows F3 at L4.
    16	
    17	**Context today (verified 28 Oct).**
    18	
    19	- OSD `origin/main` `4293cc8`: F3 is `terranubis/f3-demo-2020` (CC-BY-SA-3.0, share-alike,
    20	  registration-only, L1); `ibm-research/netherlands-f3-interpretation` (Zenodo, CC-BY-4.0,
    21	  anonymous, nine horizons as labelled images, not the cube) is a second F3 record. No pack, no
    22	  starter schema (E40), no deposit (E41) exists.
    23	- Ophiolite `origin/main` `9e34915a8`: E125 MERGED: a GPLv3 connector package over odbind gets
    24	  wells, logs, horizons, faults and a seismic cube from a project into an OpendTect survey and sends
    25	  them back, tested in CI against OpendTect 7.0.10 on Linux. E126 MERGED: lasio and pandas adapters,
    26	  a gallery of notebooks that run in CI. E85 MERGED: one intake for files, folders and archives.
    27	  E127 QUEUED: the `osd.manifest` intake and the fidelity/1 writer. Nothing in Ophiolite drives
    28	  ResInsight, and nothing writes a starter/1 document.
    29	- Non-code, read 28 Oct: dGB's F3 Demo 2023 is distributed as an OpendTect survey (project store)
    30	  behind registration; the F3 survey has four wells (F02-1, F03-2, F03-4, F06-1), inline and
    31	  crossline ranges and a 4 ms sample rate the lane freezes from the survey through odbind at lane
    32	  open. ResInsight v2026.09.1 (24 Sep 2026) ships an Ubuntu 24.04 build; its Python API `rips`
    33	  2026.9.1.2 is on PyPI and could not be installed under this host's default Python on 28 Oct
    34	  (version constraint): the lane verifies the Python it needs. OpenVDS 3.4.9, segyio 1.9.14,
